Fixture artefacts for `slurmd_differential.rs`. NOT MEASUREMENTS.

Every one of these was produced by `slurm-broker/slurmd-differential.sh` running against
`slurm-broker/slurmd-differential-fixture/sbatch`, a fake whose substitution model is a COPY
of what the operator measured by hand on Santis 2026-08-31 (`doc/review-v0.5/round3/RA.md`
§6, §7, §8). They exist so the grader can be exercised end to end with no cluster; they are
evidence about the harness and about nothing else. Their `META sbatch_version` says so, and
the grader prints `SOURCE IS NOT SLURM` for all of them.

  measured.artefact       the world the operator measured
  husk-world.artefact     a counterfactual where slurmd does exactly what husk's table says
  stepid-drift.artefact   the measured world with ONE open question resolved the other way:
                          %s renders as `0` while SLURM_STEP_ID stays unset. This is the row
                          the real cluster run exists to produce or to rule out, and it is
                          what makes the grader's DISAGREE path testable offline.
  dry-run.artefact        `--dry-run`: invocations recorded, nothing submitted
  control-failed.artefact measured.artefact with the literal-name control marked FAIL
  absent-file.artefact    measured.artefact with j01-o's file removed

Regenerate with `slurm-broker/slurmd-differential.test.sh`, which runs the harness against
the fixture and grades the result it just produced.
